  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients well. Bring to boil for 5 minutes with stirring. Allow to cool to room temperature and skim fat."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Alternatively, you may cool in a refrigerator and remove hardened fat from surface. Filter through cheese cloth and retain both meat particles and the filtrate."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Bacteriology should specify whether they want the meat particles in the final medium or not. To the filtrate, add sufficient water to restore volume to 1.0 L."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "To the retained filtrate, add:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Boil, cool, and add 0.5 grams of Cysteine."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Set pH to 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": "Dispense anaerobically under nitrogen or nitrogen:hydrogen gas. Dispense in 7 ml volumes."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "Cap with rubber stoppers and autoclave at 121 C for 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "If meat particles are required, use one part meat per 4-5 parts broth."
    }
  ]
}